DTSTAMP:20260917T172952Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53825052061495-53825052061496@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Perimenopause can bring changes in periods\, sleep\, mood\, co
 gnition\, and physical symptoms often years before the final menstrual per
 iod. Kathryne Sanserino\, MD\, FACOG\, MSCP\, will explain what happens du
 ring this transition and how symptoms can be managed. \n\nCommon symptoms 
 of perimenopause and why they happenHow menstrual cycles and bleeding patt
 erns may changeTreatment options including hormonal and non-hormonal thera
 piesSleep\, mood\, brain fog\, and other less-recognized symptomsPractical
  strate\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-17 10:29 PDT
END:VEVENT
