  (AAAI)\, offering a glimpse into one of the fastest-growing areas of the 
 museum’s collection. Many of the works on view are being presented for t
 he first time.\n\nFounded in 2018 by Stanford art history professor Marci 
 Kwon and Cantor associate curator of modern and contemporary art Aleesa Pi
 tchamarn Alexander\, the AAAI is one of the nation's leading museum initia
 ti\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/focu
 s-asian-american-art-collection\nLast synced: 2026-09-17 10:29 PDT
LOCATION:Cantor Arts Center
URL:https://museum.stanford.edu/exhibitions/focus-asian-american-art-colle
 ction
END:VEVENT
